<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 99,468 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 99,468 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 99,468 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday, compared to 64,297 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Saturday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			18,350	    15,822</p>
<p>    Import cargo			81,118	    48,475</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, eight ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, 10 ships are expected to sail and six to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	     65,000	 Capt. Miranda	   due</p>
<p>General cargo	  7,000	 Sargodha		  due</p>
<p>General cargo	  5,343	 Bolan		     22/6</p>
<p>High speed diesel   76,000	 Chesapeak City	  due</p>
<p>High speed diesel   58,000	 Al-Maqwa		  24/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
